    "Housing | Student Life | Campus Life  - CHUNG-ANG UNIVERSITY\nGo Menu\nGo Contents\nGo Footer\nCAU | CHUNG-ANG UNIVERSITY\nMenu\nGo Search\nSearch\n검색\nMost Popular Queries\nclose\nLanguage Select\nKorean\nChinese\n공유\nFaceBook\nKakao Story\ntwitter\nURL Copy\nCAU챗봇\nIntroduction\nAbout CAU\nIntroduction\n3depth\n글자 확대축소 영역\n축소\n원래대로\n확대\nPrint\nShare\nFaceBook\nKakao Story\ntwitter\nURL Copy\nExchange students are housed at the dormitories/apartments of the Seoul or Anseong campus, based on the conditions laid out in the exchange agreement.\nMoving-in and moving-out dates\nFor the spring semester : last week of February (moving in) to third week of June (moving out)\nFor the fall semester : last week of August (moving in) to the third week of December (moving out)\nThese Dates are subject to change\nUniversity dormitory\nCampus\nRoom Type\nCost per semester\nSeoul\n2 beds\n￦1,280,000(without Mealplan)\nda Vinci\n2 beds\nabout ￦800,000(without mealplan)\n*The Price is subject to change.\nSeoul dormitory - deposit (100,000 KRW)\nFacilities-Seoul Campus\nLAN and Internet access available\nStudy rooms\nComputer lab\nA weight-training center, an aerobics room\nPhone line accessible in each room\nConvenience stores in each building\nTV with access to foreign TV channels (English, German, Chinese, and Japanese), along with vending machines at the lounge\nGuide to dormitory Life\nWhen you have a problem or are encountering a difficulty, you are advised to ask your roommates or buddies for help before the dormitory supervisors. If the problem is not solved within the dormitory, you may ask the International Center for help.\nPurchase of the dormitory meal plan is mandatory.\nCompliance with the dormitory rules is required.\nNotices of the dining schedule, dormitory events, and relevant rules will be posted on the bulletin board.\nYou may also ask the dormitory supervisors for relevant information.\nFacilities-da Vinci Campus\nPC room\nReading room\nLobby\nGym(located in the Welfare Building)\nGuide to dormitory Life\nWhen you have a problem or are encountering a difficulty, you are advised to ask the floor manager or personal buddy (Global Ambassador) for help before the dormitory supervisors. If the problem is not solved within the dormitory, you may ask the International Center for help.\nPurchase of the dormitory meal plan is not mandatory. Compliance with the dormitory rules is required.\nNotices of the dining schedule, dormitory events, and relevant rules will be posted on the bulletin board.\nYou may also ask the dormitory supervisors for relevant information.\n위로\nQuick Link\nColleges\nclose\nLibraries\nSeoul Campus\nDaVinci Campus\nRelated Site\nstudy in Korea\nCollege\nHumanities\nSocial Sciences\nEducation\nNatural Sciences\nBiotechnology\nEngineering\nICT Engineering\nBusiness & Economics\nMedicine\nPharmacy\nNursing\nArt\nSport Sciences\nSoftware\nArt & Technology\nVirtual Convergence\n사이트맵\nAbout CAU\nWelcome\nPresident's Message\nPresident's Profile\nIntroduction\nIntroduction\nSymbols\nUniversity Identity\nCAU2030\nHistory\nHistory\nPresidents\nOrganization Chart\nMaps and Directions\nDirections\nCampus Shuttle Bus\nCampus Map\nVR Campus Tour\nAcademics\nAcademic Calendar\nUndergraduate School\nHumanities\nSocial Sciences\nEducation\nNatural Sciences\nBiotechnology\nEngineering\nICT Engineering\nSoftware\nBusiness & Economics\nMedicine\nPharmacy\nNursing\nArt\nArt & Technology\nSport Sciences\nGeneral Education\nVirtual Convergence\nAcademic Resources\nGraduate School\nProfessional Schools\nSpecial Graduate Programs\nCenters\nCAU Business School\nResearch\nResearch Achievements\nCurrent Status of Research Activities\nResearch Institutes\nAdmissions\nUndergraduate Admission\nGraduate Admission\nMBA\nGSIS\nKorean Language Institute\nVisa&Immigration Issues\nInternational\nParticipation in Reputation Survey\nOffice of International Affairs\nWelcome Message\nIntroduction to the Office\nOIA Staff & Contact\nInternationa